WEBVTT

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:13.730
That place...

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:17.570
...belongs to me!

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:27.110
What?

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:29.530
No, no, no, no...

00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:32.280
No, this isn't happening!

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:34.860
I didn't mean to do this!

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:38.900
Shuichi! Shuichi! Say something!

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.690
Shuichi! Shuichi! Please!

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:44.980
Shuichi, say something!

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:47.860
Shuichi! Shuichi!

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:52.440
You piece of shit!

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:10.780
Oh, Clair. It's you.

00:03:12.110 --> 00:03:17.320
Hey... Why are you inside of Shuichi?

00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:22.860
To... kill you.

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:28.110
How terrible. Your only sister...

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:34.570
Why...? Why did you kill Mom and Dad?

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:36.980
Don't you watch the news?

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:41.610
The police said it was an accident with the gas.

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:43.780
Why?!

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:47.690
I knew it'd be bad seeing you again.

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:55.110
I don't see why you had
to bring this up in front of Shuichi.

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:58.900
They were bad people.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:02.110
They were always so strict with us.

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:05.940
"Get your act together,
our family has an image to uphold."

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:10.650
Dad was a legislator,
but he did bad things behind the scenes.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:15.150
Mom had an affair with one of
the young employees at her company.

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:20.320
Even you said it:
"I'm going to kill them one day."

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:25.900
So I did it. For you.

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:33.860
I am no longer the weak sister you knew,
the one you had to protect.

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:36.110
I'm strong now.

00:04:36.110 --> 00:04:41.570
From now on, I'll protect you.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:46.480
Do you still have the coin I gave you?

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:49.440
I threw it away.

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:53.400
I'll give you another one, then.

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:59.400
Take it to the abandoned
motel along the highway.

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:05.360
Hello. It's me.

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:10.230
Okay. Yes.

00:05:10.230 --> 00:05:12.650
Got it.

00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:15.690
Sorry, Clair. Something came up.

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:19.610
Make good use of the coin, okay?

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:21.360
Seriously.

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:41.480
I'm sorry it ended this way, Shuichi.

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:45.780
But I'm going to keep my promise.

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:57.030
Nn...

00:05:57.030 --> 00:05:59.940
No! Clair!

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:03.900
Don't die, Clair!

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:07.570
Shuichi...

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:09.530
You're alive?

00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:14.070
Uh, I'm not sure that
this qualifies as "alive," but...

00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:18.030
But you can't die too!

00:06:18.030 --> 00:06:20.900
Your promise...!

00:06:21.570 --> 00:06:25.360
You're so stupid!

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:29.440
You shouldn't be worried
about others when you're like this!

00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:32.280
Clair! I can't brea--

00:06:35.820 --> 00:06:38.320
"Hotel Mythos"

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:39.750
"Running Spirit"

00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:46.280
Mmm?

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:51.570
Who are you?

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:54.150
Ooh, that looks like it hurts!

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:55.780
Huh?

00:06:57.570 --> 00:06:59.940
What happened to you?

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:01.400
Hold on!

00:07:04.780 --> 00:07:09.190
Oh, come on!
You should have told me you had a coin!

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:11.070
Ok, let me see it.

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:13.070
Stay back!

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:18.110
Hang on, Clair. This guy knows about the coins.

00:07:19.190 --> 00:07:21.360
Can you fix him?

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:24.150
I won't know until I take a look.

00:07:24.150 --> 00:07:25.360
Clair...

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:29.480
Try anything funny, and you'll regret it.

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:37.780
Hmm...

00:07:37.780 --> 00:07:43.320
No problem. I can fix him. He's still alive.

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:48.820
Well then, hand over the coin please.

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:51.530
This? I can't.

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:55.150
I need the coin to fix him.

00:07:55.730 --> 00:07:58.780
You're sure you can fix Shuichi, huh?

00:07:58.780 --> 00:08:00.570
Yes.

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:09.980
Here! Drink that.

00:08:09.980 --> 00:08:11.980
What the hell is it?

00:08:11.980 --> 00:08:15.530
It's a bit hard to explain...

00:08:15.530 --> 00:08:18.940
Sort of controlling microbes
with molecular mechanisms...

00:08:18.940 --> 00:08:24.610
Forget about the theory.
If he drinks it, his neck will reattach.

00:08:24.610 --> 00:08:28.360
What'll you do, Shuichi?

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:31.440
Okay, I'll drink it.

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:33.480
What a relief, eh?

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:39.320
If you'd gone back to your normal form
in that state, you would have died!

00:08:39.320 --> 00:08:40.730
So it's true!

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:45.980
All right, hold it down tight.

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:48.440
If you don't, it might stick on crooked.

00:09:02.070 --> 00:09:06.110
Hey, is it okay if I get out?

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:07.860
Yes, that's fine.

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:11.320
Sorry, Shuichi. You mind?

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:13.150
Go ahead.

00:09:25.820 --> 00:09:27.360
Oooh...

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:28.820
What?

00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:33.610
Well, you just have a surprisingly lovely body.

00:09:33.610 --> 00:09:37.610
You, too. You're pretty handsome, huh?

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:40.110
This body?

00:09:40.110 --> 00:09:46.730
I've simply adopted the most
suitable one for fitting in on this planet.

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:49.860
We don't actually have static forms.

00:09:49.860 --> 00:09:51.030
Huh?

00:09:51.030 --> 00:09:52.480
What do you mean?

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:58.820
Oh? Haven't you heard?
I'm what you people call an alien.

00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:00.190
What?

00:10:00.190 --> 00:10:03.280
I totally thought someone
told you before you came!

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:08.110
You'll be sure to keep my personal
information private, won't you?

00:10:12.070 --> 00:10:13.820
What are you looking at?!

00:10:13.820 --> 00:10:17.150
Well, I am certainly an alien,

00:10:17.150 --> 00:10:21.570
but physically speaking,
I'm a complete human male, so...

00:10:21.570 --> 00:10:25.690
Excuse me, might I touch them just--

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:34.820
What are you doing?!

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:37.030
Oh, sorry! Reflex!

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:43.030
Please trust me! I'm not a bad alien!

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:50.190
Here! I'll demonstrate.
Your name is Clair, right?

00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:53.070
Please give me one of
your hairs from down there.

00:10:53.070 --> 00:10:53.900
Wha--?

00:10:53.900 --> 00:10:55.150
They haven't started growing yet!

00:10:55.150 --> 00:10:56.110
What?!

00:10:56.110 --> 00:10:56.690
That's a lie.

00:10:56.690 --> 00:10:58.360
A lie?!

00:10:58.360 --> 00:11:03.980
I'm not giving a single hair off
my head to someone I don't know.

00:11:03.980 --> 00:11:06.360
Okay, that's fine.

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:09.320
I'll just used the one
I snatched when you kicked me.

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:17.070
Question: Do you like yourself?
Or do you hate yourself?

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:22.690
That's a pointless question.
You don't get to choose who you are.

00:11:22.690 --> 00:11:26.480
If you still can't find anything
at all to like about yourself...

00:11:26.480 --> 00:11:28.320
You should just die.

00:11:29.070 --> 00:11:34.900
I see. Some people wish they
were someone else, though, right?

00:11:34.900 --> 00:11:38.400
I think it could happen to just about anyone.

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:42.690
Aside from people that are
really into themselves, I guess.

00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:45.610
Don't you ever think...

00:11:47.190 --> 00:11:49.860
...you'd like to turn into someone else?

00:11:52.570 --> 00:11:54.610
You're not the slightest bit intrigued?

00:11:56.690 --> 00:12:03.400
The prospect of becoming
the person you've wanted to be...

00:12:03.400 --> 00:12:05.480
A greater version of your current self.

00:12:10.780 --> 00:12:13.570
Your body really is quite nice.

00:12:15.570 --> 00:12:19.690
I think I'll stick with it.

00:12:19.690 --> 00:12:21.530
You're not the slightest bit intrigued?

00:12:21.530 --> 00:12:25.230
A new and different version of you.

00:12:25.230 --> 00:12:31.570
I can change your life in ways
that will surely be... interesting.

00:12:31.570 --> 00:12:35.070
Just like your friend there.

00:12:35.070 --> 00:12:40.110
Was he the one that made me this way?!

00:12:40.110 --> 00:12:42.820
How did you change Shuichi into a monster?

00:12:42.820 --> 00:12:47.110
With medicine. Similar to the one he just drank.

00:12:47.110 --> 00:12:50.400
Still, calling him a monster is a little rude!

00:12:50.400 --> 00:12:55.780
That was the form he desired--his ideal form!

00:12:55.780 --> 00:13:00.900
The medicine works by changing
the body as its owner desires, you see.

00:13:00.900 --> 00:13:02.570
You've got to be joking!

00:13:02.570 --> 00:13:05.610
I never wanted to turn into this thing,

00:13:05.610 --> 00:13:09.480
and I certainly don't
remember drinking that medicine!

00:13:09.480 --> 00:13:13.860
I'm the one who made you take that form.

00:13:13.860 --> 00:13:18.280
What an incredible idea!

00:13:18.280 --> 00:13:23.650
Letting someone inside of you
to make up for your own weakness.

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:28.440
Humans really are more
imaginative than I thought.

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:34.230
It sounds like you're
the source of all this trouble.

00:13:35.070 --> 00:13:39.280
I'll accept the fact that you're an alien...

00:13:39.280 --> 00:13:41.980
...but I'd like you to drop that appearance.

00:13:41.980 --> 00:13:44.940
You're freely revealing my...
personal information.

00:13:44.940 --> 00:13:50.610
Oh, what a shame. I really liked this body.

00:13:54.820 --> 00:13:57.360
It should be okay for you to transform back now.

00:14:05.730 --> 00:14:07.650
Ah, Cla--

00:14:11.730 --> 00:14:15.780
Hey, Clair... What is it?

00:14:18.320 --> 00:14:22.820
We were on the way back to our home planet.

00:14:22.820 --> 00:14:26.730
Physical forms become a nuisance
during long trips through space,

00:14:26.730 --> 00:14:31.900
so we compressed our minds
and knowledge into data.

00:14:31.900 --> 00:14:35.070
That's what those coins are.

00:14:35.070 --> 00:14:39.530
However, our spaceship
wore down and eventually broke.

00:14:39.530 --> 00:14:42.690
We ended up crashing here.

00:14:42.690 --> 00:14:46.980
My brethren were flung
from the ship and spread out.

00:14:48.690 --> 00:14:53.900
Repairing the ship and finding my friends
are outside of my realm of expertise,

00:14:53.900 --> 00:14:58.480
so I'd like you to join the ranks of "gatherers"
that are looking for my friends.

00:14:59.650 --> 00:15:04.190
Naturally, you'll be compensated.
We'll start with a single coin.

00:15:04.190 --> 00:15:07.070
With it, I give you medicine
that lets you transform.

00:15:07.070 --> 00:15:09.780
But that's not all...

00:15:09.780 --> 00:15:14.070
If you collect 100 coins,
you can do something even more amazing!

00:15:14.070 --> 00:15:16.440
What are you talking about?

00:15:18.280 --> 00:15:20.190
Do you like comic books?

00:15:20.190 --> 00:15:21.570
Comic books?

00:15:21.570 --> 00:15:24.400
Cartoons or movies are good, too.

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:26.980
They're really entertaining, huh?

00:15:26.980 --> 00:15:30.360
I've been hooked on them since I got here.

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:32.860
Isn't it amazing?

00:15:32.860 --> 00:15:35.980
Turning into a giant and
defeating a whole city of enemies,

00:15:35.980 --> 00:15:39.530
using your own energy to destroy
a planet--they can do anything!

00:15:40.230 --> 00:15:45.650
Wouldn't it be cool if you could
turn into something like that?

00:15:48.230 --> 00:15:50.110
Let me ask you another question.

00:15:50.110 --> 00:15:51.610
What is it?

00:15:51.610 --> 00:15:55.650
Shuichi. Have you ever
picked up one of those coins before?

00:15:55.650 --> 00:15:57.110
No.

00:15:57.110 --> 00:16:02.650
Shuichi has no memory
of how he became a monster.

00:16:02.650 --> 00:16:08.280
Someone probably made him drink it
or something--you know about that?

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:13.530
Might involve a girl two years older
than me with communication problems.

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:17.400
Oh, is there really a
bad person like that out there?

00:16:17.400 --> 00:16:22.070
Anyhow, whether or not
you participate is up to you.

00:16:22.980 --> 00:16:24.280
The coin...

00:16:27.900 --> 00:16:31.900
In exchange for power, you lose everything.

00:16:33.570 --> 00:16:37.980
I see. I'll think about it.

00:16:39.820 --> 00:16:43.900
Lucky I found these sandals!

00:16:43.900 --> 00:16:48.280
You don't know my sister at all then, do you?

00:16:48.280 --> 00:16:51.070
She's the same year in school as you,

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:55.280
but she's always gone to
private schools in other areas,

00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:58.320
so it'll be hard to find out
what your connection is.

00:16:59.570 --> 00:17:03.570
That bitch did it, though.

00:17:03.570 --> 00:17:08.730
I don't know how,
but she took that medicine and--

00:17:08.730 --> 00:17:11.030
Clair, no!

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:14.360
You can't use the coin.

00:17:14.360 --> 00:17:18.110
You have another, don't you?

00:17:18.110 --> 00:17:20.980
Things keep getting worse.

00:17:20.980 --> 00:17:24.480
I've almost been killed twice
in the past two weeks.

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:27.650
And you're unable to transform.
If this keeps up--

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:29.110
You're wrong.

00:17:29.110 --> 00:17:30.400
What?!

00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:33.900
Things are much better for me now.

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:37.150
Way better than before
my sister killed our parents.

00:17:37.150 --> 00:17:42.570
Yeah... The worst of it was
just after my sister disappeared.

00:17:42.570 --> 00:17:45.940
I told people what happened,
but nobody believed me.

00:17:45.940 --> 00:17:50.280
There was no place for me in the world.

00:17:50.280 --> 00:17:54.730
But that all changed when I met you.

00:17:54.730 --> 00:17:57.610
My life seemed to start up again.

00:17:57.610 --> 00:18:02.570
And I found a place in it for me.

00:18:03.440 --> 00:18:08.440
It's really incredible!
There's an alien that gives you crazy powers,

00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:11.610
plus my sister is all wrapped up in it!

00:18:11.610 --> 00:18:15.280
I've never been so excited!

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:19.190
It's okay. I won't use the coin.

00:18:20.860 --> 00:18:24.030
I've got you.

00:18:24.030 --> 00:18:29.480
Clair and I are really are completely different.

00:18:33.360 --> 00:18:36.480
Oh my god, that's so funny!

00:18:40.530 --> 00:18:41.650
Huh?!

00:18:41.650 --> 00:18:44.360
Hey, where the hell do you think you're going?

00:18:49.530 --> 00:18:53.030
Why are you... so strong...?

00:18:53.030 --> 00:18:56.190
Hey, Kagaya! What's going on?

00:18:56.190 --> 00:18:58.610
Oh, Abukawa!

00:18:58.610 --> 00:18:59.900
Hmm?

00:19:00.730 --> 00:19:03.730
Hey, where are your glasses?

00:19:03.730 --> 00:19:05.690
I switched to contacts.

00:19:05.690 --> 00:19:08.940
Kagaya feels a bit different lately, huh?

00:19:08.940 --> 00:19:10.360
What do you mean?

00:19:10.360 --> 00:19:14.900
I guess he just seems more adult or something...

00:19:25.400 --> 00:19:27.110
What's up, Mifune?

00:19:27.110 --> 00:19:29.860
Huh? How did you...?

00:19:29.860 --> 00:19:33.070
I saw you coming up the stairs a minute ago.

00:19:33.070 --> 00:19:34.570
Oh...

00:19:34.570 --> 00:19:38.280
I wanted to give your notebook back to you.

00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:39.690
Oh.

00:19:40.860 --> 00:19:45.860
One of the girls in our class was
saying how you're kind of cool now.

00:19:46.980 --> 00:19:50.030
Your glasses weren't so bad, tho--

00:19:50.030 --> 00:19:52.780
Mifune...

00:19:52.780 --> 00:19:56.730
What would you do if
the world was going to end today?

00:19:56.730 --> 00:19:59.320
Huh? Oh, is this one of those

00:19:59.320 --> 00:20:03.360
"what would you take to
a deserted island" questions?

00:20:03.360 --> 00:20:05.190
No.

00:20:05.190 --> 00:20:09.610
What if there was someone
who didn't care about other people,

00:20:09.610 --> 00:20:13.070
and that person became incredibly powerful...

00:20:13.070 --> 00:20:19.610
So powerful that they could destroy
this town, or the entire planet.

00:20:19.610 --> 00:20:23.820
The world could end out of nowhere.

00:20:23.820 --> 00:20:26.230
With no warning.

00:20:26.230 --> 00:20:30.650
If something like that could happen today...

00:20:30.650 --> 00:20:36.650
Um... Well... I don't know,
that sounds tricky...

00:20:36.650 --> 00:20:43.570
Well, I... I guess, for me,
I'd be worried about my parents,

00:20:43.570 --> 00:20:45.780
and all my classmates...

00:20:45.780 --> 00:20:47.980
I'd try to stop the bad guy

00:20:47.980 --> 00:20:51.150
or do my best to make sure that didn't happen!

00:20:51.150 --> 00:20:54.030
Yeah. That's normal, huh?

00:20:54.030 --> 00:20:55.110
What?

00:20:55.110 --> 00:20:59.900
Thank you. I needed to hear someone say that.

00:21:01.730 --> 00:21:03.530
Later.

00:21:13.150 --> 00:21:17.400
I'm just speculating,
but it's hard to imagine that

00:21:17.400 --> 00:21:20.900
everything the alien said is true.

00:21:20.900 --> 00:21:26.940
There's some big story lurking
in the shadows of this town.

00:21:26.940 --> 00:21:32.940
And I'm pretty sure I'm not the main character.

00:21:34.150 --> 00:21:36.940
But I won't run!

00:21:39.650 --> 00:21:44.230
The spaceship went down
somewhere in those mountains.

00:21:44.230 --> 00:21:47.320
There's a good chance we'll find some coins,

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:50.940
but also a good chance
we'll run into some enemies.

00:21:51.820 --> 00:21:56.780
It's okay, Shuichi. You'll survive.

00:21:56.780 --> 00:21:58.900
I'm with you.

00:22:03.360 --> 00:22:05.860
Okay, let's go.

00:23:44.230 --> 00:23:47.030
"Episode 5: Crazy Enemies"
